\title{Talks Style Guide}
\author{Ivan Jacob Agaloos Pesigan}
\date{}

\begin{document}

\maketitle

Manuscripts are papers; talks are presentations that maximize appeal,
so they get leeway.
The rules split in two:
what is kept for correctness and reuse, and what is free.
Agents follow \texttt{.setup/ai/style/talks.md},
which follows this guide and is changed together with it.

\section{Kept}

These are checked by \texttt{make lint}, as in papers.

\begin{itemize}
	\item Math: \texttt{\textbackslash boldsymbol}, portable commands, and the shared notation,
	so that an equation pasted from a paper renders the same.
	\item R code and file names, since talks are R packages.
	\item Citations: any biblatex-apa command
	(\texttt{\textbackslash parencite}, \texttt{\textbackslash textcite},
	\texttt{\textbackslash footcite}, \texttt{\textbackslash fullcite}),
	with lib-* keys only and no typed references.
	\item One body (\texttt{.setup/latex/slides/talk.tex}) for slides, notes, and handout.
	A talk with slides only may skip the wrappers.
	\item Accessibility floor: meaning is never shown by colour alone.
	Add a shape, line type, label, or position.
\end{itemize}

\section{Free}

This is guidance, not lint.

\begin{itemize}
	\item Colours: the Penn State theme and any palette that helps the slide
	(Okabe-Ito recommended), within the floor above.
	\item Figure sizes: any; \texttt{scale} and \texttt{width} are allowed.
	\texttt{Fig*(size = "slide")} gives slide fonts.
	\item TikZ inline in frames, or from \texttt{.setup/latex/tikz}
	(recommended when a paper uses the same diagram).
	\item Layout: semantic line breaks and tabs are recommended;
	no APA captions, labels, or notes.
	\item Images and photos in PNG or JPG.
	\item GIFs: free, except the floor, no flashing faster than 3 per second, and alt text on the web.
\end{itemize}

\section{Formats}

\subsection{Beamer}

\texttt{beamerthemePSU}, with one body and three wrappers (slides, notes for pympress, handout).
Animations play with \texttt{\textbackslash PSUanimation} (PNG frames)
or \texttt{\textbackslash PSUanimationpdf} (a multi-page PDF).

\subsection{Reveal.js}

Quarto Reveal.js, from \texttt{.setup/quarto}.
Use GIFs directly and the same math (MathJax: no \texttt{\textbackslash bm}).

\section{Lifetime}

Finished talks are still checked; there is no skip after the talk's date.
Older talks follow the rules when next reused.

\section{Tools}

\texttt{make lint} uses a talk profile for project type \texttt{talk}:
it runs the kept checks and skips the free ones.

\nocite{RCoreTeam-2026}

